From a828c6d56c732f5ccc45d19cb926ecba35ffc23d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:09:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ext/soap: do not match the DTD node kept by GHSA-4646 as an
 element

The GHSA-4646-p932-gw34 fix keeps the DTD node in the document until it
is freed. That node is named after the DOCTYPE, so looking up an element
such as definitions, schema or Envelope could return the DTD node
instead, and a WSDL, schema or request with a DOCTYPE named like its root
element failed. node_is_equal_ex() now only matches element nodes.

Backport of Jakub Zelenka's follow-up to the 2026-11-19 release, with
Sury's change of its tests from --EXTENSIONS-- (not known to this
version's run-tests) to SKIPIF; same change as Sury's 5.6 patches 0410
and 0411.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
